{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"cea02c357442b8fe","name":"card_event_cobelligerents","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/WinterWar/events/card_event_cobelligerents","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CO-BELLIGERENTS","text":"Target enemy unit is shuffled into your deck.","flavorText":"In WWII, various nations and resistance movements, such as those from occupied countries or exiled governments, acted as co-belligerents, actively engaging in the fight without being formal parties of an alliance. Just as there were co-belligerents who aligned themselves and fought alongside the Allied powers (e.g. Free France, Poland, Norway, The Netherlands,Yugoslavia and Greece) there were also co-belligerents who sided with or supported the Axis powers, for exemple Finland, which switched sides and fought with the Allies against Germany from 1944. Similarly, Italy, Romania, Hungary and Bulgaria, all former allies of Germany, would later switch sides and join the Allies in the war against the nazi regime. It should also be mentioned that the pact between Germany and the Soviet Union against Poland in 1939 has been described as co-belligerent.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":7,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_cobelligerents","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_cobelligerents_title","SourceString":"CO-BELLIGERENTS","LocalizedString":"CO-BELLIGERENTS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_cobelligerents_text","SourceString":"Target enemy unit is shuffled into your deck.","LocalizedString":"Target enemy unit is shuffled into your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_cobelligerents_history","SourceString":"In WWII, various nations and resistance movements, such as those from occupied countries or exiled governments, acted as co-belligerents, actively engaging in the fight without being formal parties of an alliance. Just as there were co-belligerents who aligned themselves and fought alongside the Allied powers (e.g. Free France, Poland, Norway, The Netherlands,Yugoslavia and Greece) there were also co-belligerents who sided with or supported the Axis powers, for exemple Finland, which switched sides and fought with the Allies against Germany from 1944. Similarly, Italy, Romania, Hungary and Bulgaria, all former allies of Germany, would later switch sides and join the Allies in the war against the nazi regime. It should also be mentioned that the pact between Germany and the Soviet Union against Poland in 1939 has been described as co-belligerent.","LocalizedString":"In WWII, various nations and resistance movements, such as those from occupied countries or exiled governments, acted as co-belligerents, actively engaging in the fight without being formal parties of an alliance. Just as there were co-belligerents who aligned themselves and fought alongside the Allied powers (e.g. Free France, Poland, Norway, The Netherlands,Yugoslavia and Greece) there were also co-belligerents who sided with or supported the Axis powers, for exemple Finland, which switched sides and fought with the Allies against Germany from 1944. Similarly, Italy, Romania, Hungary and Bulgaria, all former allies of Germany, would later switch sides and join the Allies in the war against the nazi regime. It should also be mentioned that the pact between Germany and the Soviet Union against Poland in 1939 has been described as co-belligerent."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'For_the_Queen'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/For_the_Queen.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/CandidateArtwork/Winter_War/t_cobelligrent.t_cobelligrent","SubPathString":""},"a